  "narrative": "The newly delivered validation materially strengthens the central feature_063 context finding and resolves the response-deadline items.\\n\\nFirst, H115 is now independently validated. Its discovery interaction, feature_063=1 versus 0 within high feature_038 minus its low-feature_038 complement over the full eligible population, was +0.559 signed composite dependency-score units, interval +0.387 to +0.731 (R98). The independent validation is +0.544, interval +0.295 to +0.793 (R106). The independent interval is entirely above the 0.15-unit threshold and directionally consistent with discovery. Therefore I accept H115 and close it: feature_063=1 is associated with a much stronger lower outcome_001 value in the high-feature_038 half than in the low-feature_038 half, even when dominant binary-marker contexts are pooled. This is the broadest and most robust form of the feature_038 modification signal, building on the already accepted validated narrower feature_037=0/feature_010=0 interaction H103.\\n\\nSecond, H87 required explicit reassessment. Its discovery feature_063=1 versus 0 contrast within feature_037=0/feature_010=0 was +0.261, interval +0.172 to +0.350 (R67). The independent validation is +0.234, interval +0.102 to +0.365 (R79). The validation point estimate is above the threshold, excludes zero, and closely matches discovery, but the stringent independent interval has a lower bound below 0.15. I keep H87 accepted and closed as a supplied-dataset descriptive association: discovery alone provided a threshold-supported effect, and validation supports the same magnitude and direction, although the independent uncertainty is wider. This is not evidence of causality, biological mechanism, or generalization beyond the supplied dataset.\\n\\nThird, H10 and H79 scheduled validations support negative interpretations. H10 asked whether feature_007's effect differs by high versus low feature_038; discovery was near null (+0.008, -0.110 to +0.126; R10) and validation was also near null (+0.014, -0.155 to +0.183; R80). I reject and close H10. H79 asked whether feature_063's effect differs between feature_010=1 and feature_010=0 within the feature_002=0/feature_037=0 context; discovery (+0.058, -0.303 to +0.419; R60) and validation (+0.030, -0.379 to +0.438; R107) are both null-like. I reject and close H79. These results further weaken broad feature_007-by-feature_038 and feature_063-by-feature_010 interaction hypotheses.\\n\\nUpdated supported descriptive findings in this supplied dataset are: feature_037=1 is strongly associated with lower outcome_001, broadly and across many strata, including log-pfs robustness in both short and long log-pfs quartiles; feature_002=1 is strongly associated with higher outcome_001 broadly and across accepted strata; feature_010=1 is associated with higher outcome_001 broadly, with strong short-log-pfs support but only unresolved long-log-pfs subgroup certainty. feature_063=1 is most clearly associated with lower outcome_001 in contexts where feature_037 and feature_010 are absent, and especially in high-feature_038 contexts. The feature_038 modification is now robust in two complementary forms: the feature_037=0/feature_010=0 context interaction H103, and the broad overall interaction H115, both independently validated with intervals entirely above threshold. Direct accepted contrasts include high-feature_038 overall effect H113, high-feature_038 within the accepted double-negative context H105, low-feature_018 within that context H112, and accepted feature_063 strata such as H87/H90/H61/H67/H68/H92/H93/H95/H96.\\n\\nNegative or negative-like findings are now broad: the supplied binary markers feature_007, feature_058, feature_015, and feature_041 lack meaningful broad main effects; feature_007 interaction with feature_038 is null (H10 validated); feature_063 interaction with feature_010 in feature_002=0/feature_037=0 is null (H79 validated); feature_063-by-long-log-pfs interaction is unsupported (H104); feature_036 does not support a feature_063 context modification (H107); original high-feature_018 stronger feature_063 interaction H106 is rejected; low-feature_038 contexts are null or subthreshold (H94, H114, H111); and feature_010 attenuation of feature_063 within high feature_038 is unsupported (H117).\\n\\nUnresolved uncertainty remains around several smaller or sparser interactions: the reversed feature_018 context interaction H110 remains directionally suggestive but not accepted as threshold-robust because its lower bound is below threshold; broad attenuation interactions by feature_010 or feature_037 presence (H108/H109) remain wide; feature_037 attenuation within high feature_038 H116 remains unresolved; feature_002-by-feature_010 non-additivity H41 is borderline; feature_002 log-pfs robustness H99/H100 is still pending; long-pfs feature_010 effect H102 is below-threshold in lower bound; and the sparse accepted feature_037=1/feature_038 interaction H118 needs direct stratum confirmation through H119/H120. The overall feature_063 main effect H66 is likely diluted by contexts with little or no meaningful association and should not be treated as a threshold-supported broad effect without context.\\n\\nThe most informative next analyses are already registered: direct feature_063 contrasts within feature_037=1/high-feature_038 (H119) and feature_037=1/low-feature_038 (H120) to confirm whether the accepted sparse H118 interaction reflects a real direct stratum pattern; H99/H100 to complete log-pfs robustness for feature_002; and H41 follow-up if capacity remains. I additionally registered a direct high-feature_038/feature_037=0 contrast to help resolve the unresolved H116 attenuation signal. All conclusions remain descriptive associations in the supplied dataset, not causal, biological, mechanistic, or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "After iteration 8 synthesize: H115 overall feature_063-by-feature_038 interaction accepted and closed; independent validation +0.544 [0.295,0.793] entirely above threshold, discovery +0.559 [0.387,0.731]. This is the broadest validated feature_038 modification. H87 accepted/closed; discovery +0.261 [0.172,0.350], validation +0.234 [0.102,0.365] point consistent but lower below threshold, so accepted as supported descriptive association not independently threshold-complete. H10 rejected/closed; feature_007-by-feature_038 null discovery + validation. H79 rejected/closed; feature_063-by-feature_010 in feature_002=0/feature_037=0 null discovery + validation. Central accepted map: feature_037=1 lowers outcome_001 strongly (validated, log-pfs robust); feature_002=1 raises outcome_001 strongly (validated broad); feature_010=1 raises outcome_001 broadly (validated broad; short log-pfs accepted, long unresolved); feature_063=1 lowers outcome_001 mainly in feature_037=0/feature_010=0 contexts and high feature_038 contexts. Accepted feature_063 context/validated interactions: H103 (feature_038 interaction within double-negative stratum validated), H115 (overall feature_038 interaction validated), H113 high feature_038 direct accepted, H114 low feature_038 rejected null, H105 high feature_038 double-negative accepted, H94 low feature_038 double-negative rejected null, H112 low feature_018 double-negative accepted, H111 high feature_018 rejected subthreshold, H93 residual high feature_038 accepted, H92 long log-pfs residual accepted but sparse, H61/H67 validated feature_063 strata. Negative broad: feature_007/058/015/041 main effects null; H10 null; H79 null; H117 feature_010 attenuation in high feature_038 null; H104 long log-pfs feature_063 interaction null; H107 feature_036 null; H106 high feature_018 direction rejected; H94/H114 low feature_038 null. Unresolved: H110 reversed feature_018 interaction suggestive +0.272 [0.099,0.445]; H116 feature_037 attenuation high feature_038 +0.101 [-0.175,0.376]; H108/H109 broad attenuation wide; H41 feature_002-by-feature_010 +0.210 [0.019,0.400]; H66 overall feature_063 diluted; H88/H89 broader feature_063 contexts; H102 long log-pfs feature_010 +0.290 [0.068,0.511]; H99/H100 pending; H118 accepted but sparse feature_037=1/feature_038 interaction needs direct confirmation. Next analyze priorities: H119/H120 direct feature_063 within feature_037=1/high and low feature_038, new H121 direct feature_063 within high feature_038/feature_037=0, then H99/H100 feature_002 log-pfs robustness, then H41 follow-up if capacity. Do not treat overall H66 or H110 as accepted threshold claims. All conclusions descriptive supplied-dataset associations, not causal, biological, mechanistic, or generalizable."
